{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 28, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "מלואים", :translit "milu'im", :gloss "inauguration offerings"} {:he "נהפך להם לתוגה", :translit "nehepach lahem latugah", :gloss "it turned for them into mourning"} {:he "שמתו נדב ואביהוא", :translit "shemetu nadav va'avihu", :gloss "when Nadav and Avihu died"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "Defective spelling of מלואים (missing ו/yod) signals diminution, foreboding the deaths of Nadav and Avihu on the inauguration day"}], :frame {:text "On the day of the Tabernacle's inauguration, Nadav and Avihu offered unauthorized fire before God and were consumed by divine fire (Leviticus 10:1–2). Their death transformed what should have been a day of supreme joy into one of mourning. The same term מלואים marks both the consecration of the priests (Leviticus 8:28) and the context of the tragedy that followed (Leviticus 8:33–35).", :sources ["Leviticus 10:1-2" "Leviticus 8:33-35"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :other, :note "Defective spelling of מלואים (missing ו/yod) signals diminution, foreboding the deaths of Nadav and Avihu on the inauguration day", :by :selah, :ran? false}], :book :leviticus, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 8, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:22:15.496450890Z", :model "glm-5.2"}